ion is always opposing the motion  so when the block is sliding up the  kinetic friction is down and all that we  have is a sign change here this is now  plus if I choose my I hat and J hat in  the same direction notice both of these  forces have a positive component in the  I hat direction so the acceleration will  be down and rather than do all the  algebra all I'm doing is changing the  sign and I get that a up is equal to G  sine theta plus mu K cosine theta and  although it may seem slightly  counterintuitive that the acceleration  as the block is going up in magnitude is  bigger than the acceleration as the  block is going down and that's because  of the direction of the kinetic friction  force
 

